- op: discuss  # 9b2f
  at: '2026-06-02T20:45:43Z'  # 9b2f
  by: agent  # 9b2f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9b2f
  clock: 6  # 9b2f
  nonce: 9b2f  # 9b2f
  message: "Pass 36 (continuing 06022026_1622) verify-claims YAML input format inconsistency.\n\nF36.D2 (NEW BUG): verify-claims --claims accepts EITHER top-level list YAML or dict-with-claims-key YAML, with no documented preference. Dict-format YAML (claims: [list]) works correctly; list-format YAML (bare top-level list of claim records) crashes with unhandled AttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'get' at packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/verify_claims.py:201 in load_claims:\n  for entry in data.get('claims', []):\n                ^^^^^^^^\nRoot cause: yaml.safe_load() returns whatever the YAML root is (list or dict); load_claims assumes dict and calls .get() without a type check.\n\nSame exception-handler-missing family as INV-zurih's existing scope (verify-claims raises unhandled Python traceback on malformed YAML claims file). F36.D2 is a NEW sub-axis: input shape is ALSO not validated — accepted formats are undocumented, and one of them silently crashes. Fix candidates: (a) accept BOTH formats (auto-detect list vs dict); (b) accept ONLY dict and raise a clear 'expected top-level claims: key' error at load time; (c) accept ONLY list and raise a clear error at load time. --help should document which format is accepted."  # 9b2f
- op: discuss  # ee4c
  at: '2026-06-03T00:12:41Z'  # ee4c
  by: agent  # ee4c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ee4c
  clock: 7  # ee4c
  nonce: ee4c  # ee4c
  message: "Pass-40 F40.B5 — verify-claims --claims 9-shape matrix (5 NEW unhandled-traceback shapes beyond F36.D2 list-root).\n\nverify-claims input shape matrix (9 cells):\n| shape | rc | tb | result |\n| missing path | 1 | 0 | clean 'Claims file not found' |\n| empty YAML | 0 | 0 | 'No claims found in file' |\n| scalar ('hello') | 1 | **1** | AttributeError: 'str' has no '.get' |\n| claims: null | 1 | **1** | TypeError: NoneType not iterable |\n| claims: ~ | 1 | **1** | same TypeError |\n| {} | 0 | 0 | 'No claims found in file' |\n| claims: [] | 0 | 0 | 'No claims found in file' |\n| binary file | 1 | **1** | yaml.reader.ReaderError: unacceptable character #x0000 |\n| directory path | 1 | **1** | IsADirectoryError from open() |\n\n5 NEW unhandled-traceback shapes beyond F36.D2's already-filed list-root case:\n1. scalar YAML root → AttributeError (str.get) — verify_claims.py:201\n2. claims: null → TypeError NoneType iter — verify_claims.py:201 (data.get returns None which propagates)\n3. claims: ~ → same path as null per YAML 1.2 spec for tilde\n4. binary file → yaml.reader.ReaderError leaks from PyYAML 5 layers deep\n5. directory path → IsADirectoryError from open() — no isdir check at file-load layer\n\nNotable asymmetry: empty_dict {} and claims: [] give clean rc=0 'No claims found' but their semantic siblings claims: null and claims: ~ traceback. All four are reasonable YAML representations of 'no claims' but only 2 are handled.\n\nFix-path at one location: dict-coerce + .get + null-check at load_claims:200-201 + isdir/binary-magic check at the open() layer. Combined with F36.D2 list-root case, INV-zurih scope now covers 6 distinct unhandled YAML shapes."  # ee4c
